    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and tested. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** The `frai gate init --ci` command was creating `FRAI-SPEC.md` but not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `gate` command handler in the frai CLI was using Commander.js's `args` parameter, which only captures positional arguments and ignores options (flags starting with `--`). The `--ci` flag was being silently dropped before reaching the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Fix:** Modified the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to use the raw `process.argv` slice instead of the parsed `args` parameter. This preserves all arguments and flags passed after the `gate` command.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Lines 753-754: Extract the raw argv slice starting from the 'gate' command\n- Line 755: Pass the complete `gateArgv` to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Tested `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`\n- \u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created successfully\n\nThe fix is minimal and focused\u2014it only changes how arguments are passed through without modifying the frai-gate package itself, as requested.",
